## The fraction-free column scale Lambda (the lcm of the charge denominators; refused above 2^31 - 1)
u+d: Lambda = 1 (admitted; Lambda^2 = 1.000e+00)
u+d+s: Lambda = 61 (admitted; Lambda^2 = 3.721e+03)
u+d+s+c: Lambda = 151,951 (admitted; Lambda^2 = 2.309e+10)
u+d+s+c+b: Lambda = 621,935,443 (admitted; Lambda^2 = 3.868e+17)
u+d+s+c+b+t: Lambda = 210,034,440,390,973 (REFUSED at load; Lambda^2 = 4.411e+28)

## The transformations of the weak force at the quark level: the content R the W (or the beta) carries
(the charge balance of note 36 (iii): rho_into x (M - R) + c_W = rho_from x M, so R = M_from - M_into)
d -> u + W: R = 9 - 4 = 5 units; the W's whole charge -7344; payable
s -> u + W: R = 183 - 4 = 179 units; the W's whole charge -7344; payable
c -> s + W: R = 2491 - 183 = 2308 units; the W's whole charge 7344; payable
b -> c + W: R = 8186 - 2491 = 5695 units; the W's whole charge -7344; payable
t -> b + W: R = 337711 - 8186 = 329525 units; the W's whole charge 7344; payable
u -> d + W: R = 4 - 9 = -5 units; the W's whole charge 7344; REFUSED (R below 1: the body would have to gain content, which no become does)
the register's neutron (series J): n 1839 -> p 1836 with the beta's content 3 = 1839 - 1836, the same balance at the nucleon level

# 2. The push between two quark bodies (u: 4 units + 1 glue; d: 9 units + 1 glue; release [1, 1]; the 290 fan)
u: held {'u': 4, 'glue': 1}: M 5, Q (4896, 1), G (10000, 1); Q^2 23,970,816; G^2 + M^2 100,000,025
d: held {'d': 9, 'glue': 1}: M 10, Q (-2448, 1), G (10000, 1); Q^2 5,992,704; G^2 + M^2 100,000,100
the symmetric form within the reach: push on A from B = (Q_A Q_B - G_A G_B - M_A M_B) x U(r) per unit per direction
(a negative x component on a reader at (r, 0, 0) is toward the emitter: attraction)

