# 6. The tower, the group on the three events, the regime
## The column vector of the set as the exact rational sum over its members (content, charge, strong)
  proton u u d: the members [(5, (4896, 1), (10000, 1)), (5, (4896, 1), (10000, 1)), (10, (-2448, 1), (10000, 1))]; the set (20, (7344, 1), (30000, 1))
  neutron u d d: the members [(5, (4896, 1), (10000, 1)), (10, (-2448, 1), (10000, 1)), (10, (-2448, 1), (10000, 1))]; the set (25, (0, 1), (30000, 1))
  the register's rows: the proton (1837, (7344, 1), (10000, 1)), the neutron (1840, (0, 1), (10000, 1))
  the charge composes exactly; the content and the strong charge compose to the declared sums, not to the register's rows

## The stabiliser of each shape in the cube's group of 48, and the group it induces on the three events
  the line centred at the origin: 16 of the 48 keep the set; the induced permutations of the three events: 2 ([(0, 1, 2), (2, 1, 0)])
  the corner about its corner: 4 of the 48 keep the set; the induced permutations of the three events: 2 ([(0, 1, 2), (2, 1, 0)])
  the triangle of the face-diagonal sublattice: 6 of the 48 keep the set; the induced permutations of the three events: 6 ([(0, 1, 2), (0, 2, 1), (1, 0, 2), (1, 2, 0), (2, 0, 1), (2, 1, 0)])
  S_3 on three events is carried by the 48 only on the triangle; a line or a corner carries Z_2 (the middle fixed)

